      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the slope of the line passing through two points, we use the formula: slope = (change in y) / (change in x).\n\nThe change in y is the difference between the y-coordinates of the two points: -5 - 5 = -10.\n\nThe change in x is the difference between the x-coordinates of the two points: 2 - (-3) = 5.\n\nSo, the slope of the line is -10 / 5 = -2.\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line passing through $(-3,5)$ and $(2,-5)$ is $\\boxed{-2}$.",
